<title>INDIA: India imposes ceiling on wheat product exports.</title>
<headline>India imposes ceiling on wheat product exports.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's Commerce Ministry said on Tuesday it had amended its export policy to impose a ceiling of 150,000 tonnes on exports of wheat products until the end of March, 1997.</p>
<p>The ministry introduced the change in a five-year export-import policy that covers the period to March 31, 1997.</p>
<p>&quot;Export of wheat products has been brought under ceiling for the remaining period of the current year effective 1.10.96 to 31.3.97 to ensure domestic availability,&quot; the ministry said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;The situation would be reviewed after some time when the wheat production figures for the current year (1996/97) become available and if required a decision would be taken to increase the ceiling,&quot; the statement added.</p>
</text>
